61	/**
62	 * Business Email — mailbox hosting per registered domain.
63	 *
64	 * An `EmailPlan` is a pricing tier (N mailboxes, GB/mailbox, price, term). A
65	 * customer subscribes one of their own domains to a tier (`EmailSubscription`),
66	 * which debits the wallet, then manages individual `Mailbox` rows under it.
67	 *
68	 * Mail delivery runs through a self-hosted Mailcow server, reached via lib/mailcow.ts
69	 * (config from MAILCOW_API_URL / MAILCOW_API_KEY). Creating a Mailbox row records
70	 * intent (status PROVISIONING); we then attempt to provision the real mailbox on
71	 * Mailcow and flip the row to ACTIVE, or FAILED if the call errors. All Mailcow
72	 * calls are additive and failure-tolerant — a Mailcow outage never breaks the
73	 * order flow; the row persists and can be retried via retryMailboxProvision.
74	 *
75	 * This module owns:
76	 *   - orderEmailHosting (customer subscribe)
77	 *   - addMailbox / removeMailbox / retryMailboxProvision (customer mailbox management)
78	 *   - adminSaveEmailPlan / adminToggleEmailPlan / adminDeleteEmailPlan (CRUD)
79	 */
